# Suppressions verified against the GitHub Advisory API directly (`gh api
# /advisories/<id>`), not just assumed — each entry below names the exact
# fixed version and the already-installed one. Re-check before extending
# this file: an ignore here is a claim "already patched", not "don't care".

# GHSA-3f6p-5ww8-9rcr — mysql2 auth-plugin downgrade (mysql_clear_password
# leaks credentials in plaintext). Transitive-only, via `prisma`'s own
# dependency — this project only ever connects to PostgreSQL, never MySQL.
# Advisory: first_patched_version 3.22.0. Installed (package.json
# "overrides", bun.lock): 3.23.1. Published 2026-09-01 — Trivy flagged this
# on the first scan against a freshly downloaded vulnerability DB, with an
# already-patched version installed; a scanner false positive, not a real
# gap. Delete this line once a later Trivy DB run stops flagging it.
GHSA-3f6p-5ww8-9rcr

# GHSA-ggr8-5vv4-36mx / CVE-2026-40345 — deepmerge-ts stack exhaustion on a
# crafted recursive object graph. Transitive-only, via `@prisma/config`
# (read by the `prisma` CLI, not by the running app). Advisory:
# first_patched_version 8.0.0. Installed (package.json "overrides",
# bun.lock): 8.0.0 — the exact patched version. Published 2026-08-17, same
# false-positive class as the mysql2 entry above.
GHSA-ggr8-5vv4-36mx
CVE-2026-40345
